@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.integration"

Feature:  Dossiera To Koroneiki Partner Integration
	Testing to assure dossiera to koroneiki partner account integration works properly.

Setup:
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | par.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | par.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PAR                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORPAR |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| par.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| par.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| par.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| par.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Korpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| KORPAR |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| par.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Korpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Create partner account
	Testing the ability to create a partner in Dossiera and verifying that the respective entities get sent to and created in Koroneiki

	Given I publish a partner account RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Professional Services (Technical/Web/IT)   |
	| Owner Email Address                    | par.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PAR                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Name                           | Service Partnership                        |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}" and the following values
	| Code                  | KORPAR                               | |
	| Contact Email Address | par.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Name                  | Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}        | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	And I should be able to view a postal address on koroneiki for the account "Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}" with the street address "456 Fake Street" with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 456 Fake Street |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraAccountKey}" and domain "salesforce" should be present on the account "Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraAccountKey}" and domain "dossiera" should be present on the account "Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}" should be present on the product purchase made by account "Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}" for the product "Service Partnership" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                        |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey} |
	| Entity Name | opportunity                       |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Service Partnership" and the following values
	| Name | Service Partnership | |
	And the external link with the entity id "Service Partnership" should be present on the product "Service Partnership" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera            |
	| Entity Id   | Service Partnership |
	| Entity Name | product             |
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}" for the product "Service Partnership" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |